176 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Dear Hiring Team\054\nBitpanda\047s design system role caught my attention\056 A platform serving first\055time investors and active traders across crypto\054 stocks\054 and commodities on web and native\056 That\047s a system with real surface area\056 Different user contexts\054 shared components underneath\056 Getting that to work consistently at scale is the kind of problem I find genuinely interesting\056\nI\047ve built two production systems from scratch in the past four years\056 At Abacum I defined the token architecture and governance across squads for a fintech data platform\054 and built the full engineering pipeline alongside a dedicated engineer\072 Token Studio and Style Dictionary for token export\054 a GitHub submodule connected to an npm package\054 ESLint rules for adoption enforcement\054 Storybook in Chromatic for visual regression\056 At Remuner I did the same as the sole designer\054 this time applying a lesson from Abacum\072 start with a deliberately small token set\056 A minimal set is easier to govern and easier to scale than a comprehensive one that never gets adopted\056 In both cases\054 engineers consumed updates without needing to involve design\056\nWhat I find most interesting about this role is the advocacy side\056 Getting a design system used is a different problem from building one\056 At Abacum I put together the business case with the head of design\054 presented it to engineering leadership\054 and ran Maker Days to drive adoption across squads\056 That work sits between design and engineering in a way that requires knowing both sides well enough to be credible with each\056\nI\047d be glad to walk you through the cases in more detail\056 The design systems case is at https\072\057\057manel\055leiva\056com\057cases\057design\055systems\056)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 175 0 R
     /Pg 170 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

